==Trivia==
*[[Marshmallow Cat (Rare Cat)|Marshmallow Cat]] had a third form in this game, unlike in [[The Battle Cats]].
*[[Moneko (Special Cat)|Moneko]] had a third form years prior to the introduction of Superstar Moneko, although it was just a simple palette-swap with two more lights added to her stage.
*[[Dom Cat (Special Cat)|Dom Cat]], [[Bondage Cat (Special Cat)|Bondage Cat]], [[Kung Fu Cat (Special Cat)|Kung Fu Cat]], [[Moneko (Special Cat)|Moneko]], [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Flower Cat]], [[Onmyoji Cat (Rare Cat)|Onmyoji Cat]], [[Shaman Cat (Rare Cat)|Shaman Cat]] and [[Cat Machine (Uber Rare Cat)|Cat Machine]] would go on to retain their color schemes in [[Go! Go! Pogo Cat]].
**[[Witch Cat (Rare Cat)|Witch Cat]] was less fortunate: in Nyanko Defence Force she had a black hat and brown hair, but in [[Battle Cats Quest]] it was changed to a purple hat and blonde hair.
*Christmas Neneko was the only support character who wasn't a pre-existing unit.
*Some units had different rarities than in The Battle Cats. For instance, [[Reindeer Fish Cat (Rare Cat)|Reindeer Fish Cat]] was set as an [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cat]] meanwhile it is a [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare Cat]] in [[The Battle Cats]].
*The Dark UFO Peng's yellow eyebrows referenced the eyebrow-like yellow crests of [[wikipedia:Crested penguin|crested penguins]] such as the [[wikipedia:Fiordland penguin|Fiordland penguin]], [[wikipedia:Erect-crested penguin|erect-crested penguin]] and [[wikipedia:Western rockhopper penguin|western rockhopper penguin]].
*The [[Media:StoneFace.png|stone bust]] of [[The Face]] may have been a visual pun on a [[wikipedia:Rock face|rock face]] or the term ''stone-faced''.

